1. ab#-ba ki re-a-še₃ dumu-ni-ir kiŋ₂ bi₂-in-gi₄
#lem: abba[father]; ki[place]; re[that]; dumu[child]; kiŋ[work]; gi[turn]
#tr.en: A father sent a message to his son, to a far-off place; at that time the son, 
#etcsl: line-id=1

2. dumu ki ba₉-ra₂ ŋen-na re ud-ba ba-ra-an-bad
#lem: dumu[child]; ki[place]; bad[open]; ŋen[go]; re[that]; ud[sun]; bad[open]
#tr.en: having gone to a distant place, was far away. 
#etcsl: line-id=2

3. ab-ba %e uru₂{ki}-a %s tuš-a-ra tur₅-ra gaba ba-ri
#lem: abba[father]; uru[city]; tuš[sit (down)]; tur[ill]; gaba[breast]; ri[impose]
#tr.en: The city-dwelling father was stricken with illness. 
#etcsl: line-id=3

4. sud-aŋ₂ kal-la kur sud-da pad₃-da tur₅-ra gaba ba-ri
#lem: sud[distant]; kal[rare]; kur[mountain(s)]; sud[distant]; pad[find]; tur[ill]; gaba[breast]; ri[impose]
#tr.en: He, precious brilliance found in a distant mountain (?), was stricken with illness. 
#etcsl: line-id=4

5. KA DIM₃ sag₉-sag₉ lu₂ inim zil₂-zil₂-le tur₅-ra gaba ba-ri
#lem: X; X; sag[good]; lu[person]; inim[word]; zil[good]; tur[ill]; gaba[breast]; ri[impose]
#tr.en: He, attractive in ……, a man who made words pleasing, was stricken with illness. 
#etcsl: line-id=5

6. alan sud tuku saŋ-du tuku teš₂-bi tur₅-ra gaba ba-ri
#lem: alan[image]; sud[distant]; tuku[acquire]; saŋdu[head]; tuku[acquire]; teš[unity]; tur[ill]; gaba[breast]; ri[impose]
#tr.en: He who had a tall figure, and altogether was powerful, was stricken with illness. 
#etcsl: line-id=6

7. gal-zu ŋiš-hur-ra me-te unken-na tur₅-ra gaba ba-ri
#lem: galanzu[wise]; ŋešhur[plan]; mete[appropriate thing]; unkin[assembly]; tur[ill]; gaba[breast]; ri[impose]
#tr.en: He, wise in divine plans and an ornament of the assembly, was stricken with illness. 
#etcsl: line-id=7

8. lu₂ gen₆-na ni₂ teŋ₃-ŋe₂₆ diŋir-bi tur₅-ra gaba ba-ri
#lem: lu[person]; gin[confirm]; ni[fear]; teŋ[approach]; diŋir[deity]; tur[ill]; gaba[breast]; ri[impose]
#tr.en: He who was a man of truth, god-fearing, was stricken with illness. 
#etcsl: line-id=8

9. tur₅-ra u₂ nu-gu₇ gaba ba-ri tur₅-ra ba-an-dab₅
#lem: tur[ill]; u[plant(s)]; gu[eat]; gaba[breast]; ri[impose]; tur[ill]; dab[seize]
#tr.en: He, not eating, was stricken with illness and was languishing away (?). 
#etcsl: line-id=9

10. ka u₃-ba-e-šu₂ ninda nu-mu-un-šu₂-šu₂ šag₄-sug₄-ga ba-an-nu₂
#lem: kag[mouth]; šuš[cover]; ninda[bread]; šuš[cover]; šagsug[empty]; nud[lie down]
#tr.en: Having closed his mouth, he ate no food and lay famished. 
#etcsl: line-id=10

